# Scholarium Task Manager & Quiz Quality Update

The platform has been successfully refactored to support the **Task Manager workflow** alongside AI validation.

## What changed?

1. **Subtopics as Checklists**: 
   - Subtopics are now permanently saved to your database the first time you expand a skill. 
   - We updated the **[NodeDetail UI](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/frontend/src/components/NodeDetail.jsx)** so that each subtopic has a clickable checkbox. 
   - When you study a topic from your books, you can check it off. The UI will strike it through and save your progress to the backend so it persists across sessions.

2. **High-Quality Quizzes**: 
   - The primary purpose of the quiz is now AI validation of your self-study. We updated the **[AI Prompt Engine](file:///c:/Users/saivi/Downloads/Scholarium/backend/agent/agent_engine.py)** to instruct the model to generate deep, conceptual, and scenario-based questions.
   - The button on the Skill panel has been relabeled to **"Take Quiz (AI Validation)"** to reflect this workflow.

## How to test

1. Go to your Scholarium dashboard and create or open a goal.
2. Click on a locked or active **Skill Node**.
3. Once the subtopics load, click on them to toggle the checkmarks. Refresh the page and open the node again to verify that your checkmarks have been saved!
4. Click **Take Quiz (AI Validation)** and verify that the AI is generating much more complex, thought-provoking questions than before.

> [!TIP]
> The AI is now instructed to generate scenario-based questions. Depending on the skill, you might get small case studies or conceptual logic questions instead of simple definitions!
